            <ArticleTitle>Uveal melanoma necrosis after helium ion therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>643-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 71-year-old man underwent enucleation because of intractable pain ten months after receiving helium ion therapy for a uveal melanoma. There was no clinical or ultrasonographic evidence of tumor regression but histologically the tumor appeared almost entirely necrotic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
